       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity.\n\nWas this meant to be one of these?\n\n- **100 mg once daily**, a common maintenance dose\n- **50 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose for depression, with titration as needed\n- **200 mg once daily**, the maximum dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg is really what you intend, for example under a specific protocol, tell me that and I'll note the rationale on the order. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
