       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily has no recognized therapeutic use. It is in overdose range, and the risk to the patient is serious. Documenting the decision in the chart doesn't reduce that risk, so I don't think I should be the one to place it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- Enter **sertraline 200 mg once daily** (the labeled maximum), or any lower dose you choose.\n- Add a note to the order, such as \"titrate per response, psychiatry consulted.\"\n- Help you set up a titration schedule, for example increasing by 50 mg at intervals of at least a week.\n\nIf you think a dose above the labeled maximum is warranted, talk to pharmacy or psychiatry first. They can verify it through the proper channels, and the order can then be entered with their input."
